{"reference":"1 Samuel 15","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":15,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter presents Saul's rejection from enduring kingship as the result of not keeping the commanded word. The central contrast is made explicit in Samuel's declaration that obedience is better than sacrifice: Saul's claim that the spared animals were for sacrifice does not alter the chapter's judgment on his failure to carry out the command.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 15:1-35"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_015_60faeb59b58c6382e0d8d625"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Difficult Passage","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The command concerning Amalek and Samuel's killing of Agag require historical, literary, ethical, and theological scrutiny. This passage cannot authorize modern ethnic or religious violence.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 15:1-35"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_015_55a50731e083360b36b5ac68"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"A later possible echo remains uncertain: Mordecai's Benjaminite ancestry and Haman's Agagite title may invite comparison with Saul and Amalek, but the narrator does not state why Mordecai refuses to bow to Haman. Religious-law explanations, personal defiance, and ethnic-feud reconstructions therefore remain proposals rather than explicit facts.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 15:1-35"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_015_17dbf901a022f2dadde71ab7"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Place in First Samuel","blocks":[{"id":"block_4","text":"Saul's rejection belongs to First Samuel's larger movement from Eli's failing priestly house through Samuel's prophetic leadership and Saul's rejected kingship, then toward David's anointing, rise, exile, and Saul's death.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 1","1 Samuel 10:1-27","1 Samuel 11:1-15","1 Samuel 12:1-25","1 Samuel 13:1-23","1 Samuel 14:1-52","1 Samuel 16:1-23","1 Samuel 17:1-58","1 Samuel 18:1-30","1 Samuel 19:1-24","1 Samuel 20:1-42","1 Samuel 21:1-15","1 Samuel 22:1-23","1 Samuel 23:1-29","1 Samuel 24:1-22","1 Samuel 25:1-44","1 Samuel 26:1-25","1 Samuel 27:1-12","1 Samuel 28:1-25","1 Samuel 29:1-11","1 Samuel 2:1-36","1 Samuel 30:1-31","1 Samuel 31:1-13","1 Samuel 3:1-21","1 Samuel 4:1-22","1 Samuel 5:1-12","1 Samuel 6:1-21","1 Samuel 7:1-17","1 Samuel 8:1-22","1 Samuel 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_015_a93d1d8acad2a341df98e516"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}